    'At the lesser end of the scale, an attacker may be able to leverage this vulnerability to perform virtual defacement of the website, such as changing text or images that are displayed on a particular page. However, attacks can be more severe. For example, if the attacker is able to change the [[C0]] property of an element, they could potentially induce the user to perform unintended actions by importing a malicious JavaScript file.' => 'Pada tingkat ringan, penyerang dapat melakukan defacement virtual pada situs, seperti mengubah teks atau gambar di halaman tertentu. Namun serangannya bisa jauh lebih parah. Misalnya, jika penyerang dapat mengubah properti [[C0]] suatu elemen, mereka berpotensi memicu pengguna menjalankan aksi tidak diinginkan dengan mengimpor file JavaScript berbahaya.',
    'Which sinks can lead to DOM-data manipulation vulnerabilities?' => 'Sink apa saja yang dapat memicu manipulasi data DOM?',
    'The following are some of the main sinks that can lead to DOM-data manipulation vulnerabilities:' => 'Berikut beberapa sink utama yang dapat memicu kerentanan manipulasi data DOM:',
    'How to prevent DOM-data manipulation vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah kerentanan manipulasi data DOM',
    'In addition to the general measures described on the [[A0]]DOM-based vulnerabilities[[/A0]] page, you should avoid allowing data from any untrusted source to be dynamically written to DOM-data fields. Note that Burp Suite automatically identifies this issue using static code analysis, which may lead to false positives that are not actually exploitable. The relevant code and execution paths should be reviewed to determine whether this vulnerability is indeed present, or whether mitigations are in place that would prevent exploitation.' => 'Selain langkah umum pada halaman [[A0]]Kerentanan berbasis DOM[[/A0]], hindari membiarkan data dari sumber tidak tepercaya ditulis secara dinamis ke field data DOM. Perlu dicatat bahwa alat analisis kode statis otomatis dapat melaporkan temuan positif palsu yang sebenarnya tidak dapat dieksploitasi. Kode dan alur eksekusi terkait tetap harus ditinjau untuk memastikan apakah kerentanan benar ada atau sudah dimitigasi.',

    // client-side-xpath-injection
    'DOM-based client-side XPath injection' => 'Injeksi XPath sisi klien berbasis DOM',
    "In this section, we'll look at what DOM-based XPath-injection is, discuss the potential impact of this kind of vulnerability, and suggest ways to reduce your exposure to them." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami membahas apa itu injeksi XPath berbasis DOM, dampak potensialnya, dan cara mengurangi risiko kerentanan tersebut.',
    'What is DOM-based XPath injection?' => 'Apa itu injeksi XPath berbasis DOM?',
    'DOM-based XPath-injection vulnerabilities arise when a script incorporates attacker-controllable data into an XPath query. An attacker may be able to use this behavior to construct a URL that, if visited by another application user, will trigger the execution of an arbitrary XPath query, which could cause different data to be retrieved and processed by the website.' => 'Kerentanan injeksi XPath berbasis DOM muncul saat skrip menyisipkan data yang dikendalikan penyerang ke dalam query XPath. Penyerang dapat menyusun URL yang, jika dikunjungi pengguna aplikasi lain, memicu eksekusi query XPath sembarang sehingga data berbeda diambil dan diproses oleh situs.',
    'What is the impact of DOM-based XPath injection?' => 'Apa dampak injeksi XPath berbasis DOM?',
    "Depending on the purpose for which the query results are used, it may be possible for the attacker to subvert the website's logic or cause unintended actions on behalf of the user." => 'Bergantung bagaimana hasil query tersebut dipakai, penyerang dapat membelokkan logika situs atau menyebabkan aksi yang tidak diinginkan atas nama pengguna.',
    'Which sinks can lead to XPath-injection vulnerabilities?' => 'Sink apa saja yang dapat memicu injeksi XPath?',
    'The following are some of the main sinks that can lead to DOM-based XPath-injection vulnerabilities:' => 'Berikut beberapa sink utama yang dapat memicu kerentanan injeksi XPath berbasis DOM:',
    'How to prevent DOM-based XPath-injection vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah kerentanan injeksi XPath berbasis DOM',
    'In addition to the general measures described on the [[A0]]DOM-based vulnerabilities[[/A0]] page, you should avoid allowing data from any untrusted source to be incorporated into XPath queries.' => 'Selain langkah umum pada halaman [[A0]]Kerentanan berbasis DOM[[/A0]], hindari membiarkan data dari sumber tidak tepercaya masuk ke dalam query XPath.',

    // client-side-sql-injection
    'DOM-based client-side SQL injection' => 'SQL injection sisi klien berbasis DOM',
    "In this section, we'll discuss what DOM-based client-side SQL injection is, describe how an attacker can exploit this vulnerability, and suggest ways to reduce your exposure to this kind of attack." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami membahas apa itu SQL injection sisi klien berbasis DOM, cara penyerang mengeksploitasinya, dan cara mengurangi paparan terhadap serangan ini.',
    'What is DOM-based client-side SQL injection?' => 'Apa itu SQL injection sisi klien berbasis DOM?',
    "Client-side SQL-injection vulnerabilities arise when a script incorporates attacker-controllable data into a client-side SQL query in an unsafe way. An attacker may be able to use this vulnerability to construct a URL that, if visited by another user, will execute an arbitrary SQL query within the local SQL database of the user's browser." => 'Kerentanan SQL injection sisi klien muncul saat skrip memasukkan data yang dikendalikan penyerang ke dalam query SQL sisi klien secara tidak aman. Penyerang dapat menyusun URL yang, jika dibuka pengguna lain, mengeksekusi query SQL sembarang di database SQL lokal milik browser korban.',
    'What is the impact of DOM-based client-side SQL injection?' => 'Apa dampak SQL injection sisi klien berbasis DOM?',
    "The potential impact of the vulnerability depends on the website's usage of the SQL database. If the database is used to store sensitive data, such as messages on a social network, the attacker may be able to retrieve this data." => 'Dampak potensialnya bergantung pada pemakaian database SQL oleh situs. Jika database menyimpan data sensitif, seperti pesan pada jejaring sosial, penyerang berpotensi mengambil data tersebut.',
    "If the database is used to store pending user actions, such as outgoing messages in an email application, then the attacker may be able to modify this data and perform arbitrary actions on the user's behalf." => 'Jika database dipakai untuk menyimpan aksi pengguna yang tertunda, seperti pesan keluar pada aplikasi email, penyerang bisa memodifikasi data itu dan menjalankan aksi sembarang atas nama pengguna.',
    'Which sinks can lead to DOM-based client-side SQL-injection vulnerabilities?' => 'Sink apa saja yang memicu SQL injection sisi klien berbasis DOM?',
    'The JavaScript database function [[C0]] can lead to client-side SQL-injection vulnerabilities.' => 'Fungsi database JavaScript [[C0]] dapat memicu kerentanan SQL injection sisi klien.',
    'How to prevent DOM-based client-side SQL-injection vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah SQL injection sisi klien berbasis DOM',
    'In addition to the general measures described on the [[A0]]DOM-based vulnerabilities[[/A0]] page, you should make sure that you use parameterized queries (also known as prepared statements) for all database access. This method uses two steps to safely incorporate potentially tainted data into SQL queries:' => 'Selain langkah umum pada halaman [[A0]]Kerentanan berbasis DOM[[/A0]], pastikan Anda menggunakan parameterized query (dikenal juga sebagai prepared statements) untuk seluruh akses database. Metode ini memakai dua tahap agar data berisiko aman masuk ke query SQL:',
    'The application specifies the structure of the query, leaving placeholders for each item of user input.' => 'Aplikasi menetapkan struktur query terlebih dahulu dengan menyisakan placeholder untuk setiap input pengguna.',
    'The application specifies the contents of each placeholder. As the structure of the query has already been defined in the first step, it is not possible for malformed data in the second step to interfere with the query structure.' => 'Aplikasi lalu mengisi nilai tiap placeholder. Karena struktur query sudah dikunci pada tahap pertama, data tidak valid di tahap kedua tidak dapat mengubah struktur query.',
    'In the JavaScript [[C0]] API, parameterized items can be designated within the query string using the query character [[C1]]. For each parameterized item, an additional parameter is passed to the API containing the item\'s value. To prevent oversights occurring and avoid vulnerabilities being introduced by changes elsewhere within the code base of the application, it is strongly recommended that you parameterize every variable data item that is incorporated into database queries, even if it is not obviously tainted.' => 'Pada API JavaScript [[C0]], item berparameter ditandai dalam string query dengan karakter [[C1]]. Untuk tiap item tersebut, parameter tambahan berisi nilainya dikirim ke API. Guna menghindari kelalaian akibat perubahan di bagian kode lain, sangat disarankan memparameterisasi setiap variabel data yang masuk ke query database meskipun tampak aman.',

    // local-file-path-manipulation
    'DOM-based local file-path manipulation' => 'Manipulasi path file lokal berbasis DOM',
    "In this section, we'll talk about what DOM-based local file-path manipulation is, look at the potential impact of an attack, highlight some of the sinks that can lead to this kind of vulnerability, and suggest ways that you can reduce your exposure." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami menjelaskan manipulasi path file lokal berbasis DOM, dampak serangannya, sink yang berpotensi memicunya, serta cara mengurangi paparan risiko.',
    'What is DOM-based local file-path manipulation?' => 'Apa itu manipulasi path file lokal berbasis DOM?',
    "Local file-path manipulation vulnerabilities arise when a script passes attacker-controllable data to a file-handling API as the [[C0]] parameter. An attacker may be able to use this vulnerability to construct a URL that, if visited by another user, will cause the user's browser to open an arbitrary local file." => 'Kerentanan manipulasi path file lokal muncul ketika skrip meneruskan data yang dikendalikan penyerang sebagai parameter [[C0]] ke API pengolah file. Penyerang dapat membuat URL yang, jika dibuka pengguna lain, membuat browser korban membuka file lokal sembarang.',
    'What is the impact of DOM-based local file-path manipulation?' => 'Apa dampak manipulasi path file lokal berbasis DOM?',
    'The potential impact of this vulnerability depends on how the website uses the opened file:' => 'Dampak potensial celah ini bergantung pada cara situs memakai file yang dibuka:',
    'If the website reads data from the file, the attacker may be able to retrieve this data.' => 'Jika situs membaca isi file tersebut, penyerang berpotensi mengambil data di dalamnya.',
    'If the website writes specific data to a sensitive file, the attacker may also be able write their own data to the file, which could be the configuration file of the operating system, for example.' => 'Jika situs menulis data tertentu ke file sensitif, penyerang juga berpotensi menulis datanya sendiri ke file tersebut, misalnya file konfigurasi sistem operasi.',
    'In both of these cases, the actual exploitability of the potential vulnerability may depend on other suitable functionality being present on the website.' => 'Pada kedua skenario tersebut, kemampuan eksploitasi nyata tetap bergantung pada adanya fitur pendukung lain di situs.',
    'Which sinks can lead to DOM-based local file-path manipulation vulnerabilities?' => 'Sink apa saja yang memicu manipulasi path file lokal berbasis DOM?',
    'The following are some of the main sinks can lead to DOM-based local file path manipulation vulnerabilities:' => 'Berikut beberapa sink utama yang dapat memicu kerentanan manipulasi path file lokal berbasis DOM:',
    'How to prevent DOM-based local file-path manipulation vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah manipulasi path file lokal berbasis DOM',
    'In addition to the general measures described on the [[A0]]DOM-based vulnerabilities[[/A0]] page, you should avoid allowing data from any untrusted source to dynamically pass a filename to a file-handling API.' => 'Selain langkah umum pada halaman [[A0]]Kerentanan berbasis DOM[[/A0]], hindari membiarkan data dari sumber tidak tepercaya menentukan nama file secara dinamis ke API pengolah file.',

    // ajax-request-header-manipulation
    'DOM-based Ajax request-header manipulation' => 'Manipulasi header permintaan Ajax berbasis DOM',
    "In this section, we'll look at what DOM-based Ajax request-header manipulation is, talk about the potential impact of this kind of attack, and suggest ways to reduce your exposure to Ajax request-header manipulation vulnerabilities." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami membahas manipulasi header permintaan Ajax berbasis DOM, potensi dampak serangannya, serta cara mengurangi risiko kerentanan tersebut.',
    'What is DOM-based Ajax request-header manipulation?' => 'Apa itu manipulasi header permintaan Ajax berbasis DOM?',
    'Using Ajax enables a website to make asynchronous requests to the server so that web applications can dynamically change content on the page without the need to reload the entire page. However, Ajax request-header manipulation vulnerabilities arise when a script writes attacker-controllable data into the request header of an Ajax request that is issued using an [[C0]] object. An attacker may be able to use this vulnerability to construct a URL that, if visited by another user, will set an arbitrary header in the subsequent Ajax request. This can then be used as a starting point to chain together other kinds of attack, thereby increasing the potential severity of this vulnerability.' => 'Ajax memungkinkan situs mengirim permintaan asinkron ke server agar konten halaman berubah dinamis tanpa memuat ulang seluruh halaman. Namun kerentanan manipulasi header permintaan Ajax muncul saat skrip menulis data yang dikendalikan penyerang ke header permintaan Ajax melalui objek [[C0]]. Penyerang dapat menyusun URL yang, bila dibuka pengguna lain, menyetel header sembarang pada permintaan Ajax berikutnya. Kondisi ini kerap menjadi pijakan untuk merangkai serangan lain sehingga tingkat keparahannya meningkat.',
    'What is the impact of DOM-based Ajax request-header manipulation?' => 'Apa dampak manipulasi header permintaan Ajax berbasis DOM?',
    'The potential impact of the vulnerability depends on the role of specific HTTP headers in the server-side processing of the Ajax request. If the header is used to control the behavior that results from the Ajax request, the attacker may be able to cause the user to perform unintended actions by manipulating the header. The impact also depends on what exactly the attacker is able to inject into the headers.' => 'Dampaknya bergantung pada peran header HTTP terkait dalam pemrosesan sisi server atas permintaan Ajax tersebut. Jika header mengatur perilaku dari permintaan Ajax, penyerang dapat memicu pengguna melakukan aksi tak diinginkan dengan memanipulasi header. Dampak juga bergantung pada apa yang bisa disuntikkan penyerang ke dalam header.',
    'Which sinks can lead to DOM-based Ajax request-header manipulation vulnerabilities?' => 'Sink apa saja yang memicu manipulasi header permintaan Ajax berbasis DOM?',
    'The following are some of the main sinks can lead to DOM-based Ajax request-header vulnerabilities:' => 'Berikut beberapa sink utama yang dapat memicu kerentanan manipulasi header permintaan Ajax berbasis DOM:',
    'How to prevent DOM-based Ajax request-header manipulation' => 'Cara mencegah manipulasi header permintaan Ajax berbasis DOM',
    'In addition to the general measures described on the [[A0]]DOM-based vulnerabilities[[/A0]] page, you should avoid allowing data from any untrusted source dynamically set Ajax request headers.' => 'Selain langkah umum pada halaman [[A0]]Kerentanan berbasis DOM[[/A0]], hindari membiarkan data dari sumber tidak tepercaya menyetel header permintaan Ajax secara dinamis.',

    // link-manipulation
    'DOM-based link manipulation' => 'Manipulasi tautan berbasis DOM',
    "In this section, we'll talk about what DOM-based link manipulation is, look at the impact of an attack, and suggest ways of preventing them." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami membahas apa itu manipulasi tautan berbasis DOM, dampak serangannya, dan cara pencegahannya.',
    'What is DOM-based link manipulation?' => 'Apa itu manipulasi tautan berbasis DOM?',
    'DOM-based link-manipulation vulnerabilities arise when a script writes attacker-controllable data to a navigation target within the current page, such as a clickable link or the submission URL of a form. An attacker might be able to use this vulnerability to construct a URL that, if visited by another application user, will modify the target of links within the response.' => 'Kerentanan manipulasi tautan berbasis DOM muncul saat skrip menulis data yang dikendalikan penyerang ke target navigasi di halaman aktif, seperti tautan yang bisa diklik atau URL tujuan pengiriman form. Penyerang dapat menyusun URL yang, jika dikunjungi pengguna lain, mengubah tujuan tautan dalam respons halaman.',
    'What is the impact of a DOM-based link-manipulation attack?' => 'Apa dampak serangan manipulasi tautan berbasis DOM?',
    'An attacker may be able to leverage this vulnerability to perform various attacks, including:' => 'Penyerang dapat memanfaatkan kerentanan ini untuk melakukan berbagai serangan, di antaranya:',
    'Causing the user to be redirected to an arbitrary external URL, which could facilitate a phishing attack.' => 'Mengarahkan pengguna ke URL eksternal sembarang yang mempermudah serangan phishing.',
    'Causing the user to submit sensitive form data to a server controlled by the attacker.' => 'Membuat pengguna mengirim data form sensitif ke server yang dikendalikan penyerang.',
    'Changing the file or query string associated with a link, causing the user to perform an unintended action within the application.' => 'Mengubah file atau query string pada tautan sehingga pengguna melakukan aksi yang tidak diinginkan di dalam aplikasi.',
    'Bypassing browser anti-XSS defenses by injecting on-site links containing XSS exploits. This works because anti-XSS defenses do not typically account for on-site links.' => 'Melewati pertahanan anti-XSS browser dengan menyuntikkan tautan internal berisi payload XSS, karena filter anti-XSS umumnya tidak memblokir tautan dalam situs sendiri.',
    'Which sinks can lead to DOM-based link-manipulation vulnerabilities?' => 'Sink apa saja yang memicu manipulasi tautan berbasis DOM?',
    'The following are some of the main sinks can lead to DOM-based link-manipulation vulnerabilities:' => 'Berikut beberapa sink utama yang dapat memicu kerentanan manipulasi tautan berbasis DOM:',
    'How to prevent DOM-based link-manipulation vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah manipulasi tautan berbasis DOM',
    'In addition to the general measures described on the [[A0]]DOM-based vulnerabilities[[/A0]] page, you should avoid allowing data from any untrusted source to dynamically set the target URL for links or forms.' => 'Selain langkah umum pada halaman [[A0]]Kerentanan berbasis DOM[[/A0]], hindari membiarkan data dari sumber tidak tepercaya menentukan URL target tautan atau form secara dinamis.',

    // web-message-manipulation
    'Web message manipulation' => 'Manipulasi web message',
    "In this section, we'll explain what web-message manipulation vulnerabilities are and suggest ways to reduce your exposure to them." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami menjelaskan kerentanan manipulasi web message serta cara mengurangi risiko paparannya.',
    'What is DOM-based web message manipulation?' => 'Apa itu manipulasi web message berbasis DOM?',
    "Web message vulnerabilities arise when a script sends attacker-controllable data as a web message to another document within the browser. An attacker may be able to use the web message data as a source by constructing a web page that, if visited by a user, will cause the user's browser to send a web message containing data that is under the attacker's control. For more information about the using web messages as a source, please refer to the [[A0]]Controlling the web-message source[[/A0]] page." => 'Kerentanan web message muncul ketika skrip mengirim data yang dikendalikan penyerang sebagai pesan web ke dokumen lain di dalam browser. Penyerang dapat memanfaatkan pesan tersebut sebagai source dengan membuat halaman berbahaya yang, bila dibuka korban, memicu browser mengirim pesan web berisi data kendali penyerang. Penjelasan lebih rinci mengenai web message sebagai source tersedia di halaman [[A0]]Mengendalikan sumber web message[[/A0]].',
    'Which sinks can lead to DOM-based web-message manipulation vulnerabilities?' => 'Sink apa saja yang memicu manipulasi web message berbasis DOM?',
    'The [[C0]] method for sending web messages can lead to vulnerabilities if the event listener for receiving messages handles the incoming data in an unsafe way.' => 'Metode [[C0]] untuk mengirim pesan web dapat memicu kerentanan bila event listener penerima menangani data masuk secara tidak aman.',
    'How to prevent DOM-based web message manipulation' => 'Cara mencegah manipulasi web message berbasis DOM',
    'In addition to the general measures described on the [[A0]]DOM-based vulnerabilities[[/A0]] page, you should avoid sending web messages that contain data that originated from any untrusted source. When sending cross-origin messages, you should always explicitly specify the target window. Most importantly, make sure to implement robust measures to verify the origin of any incoming messages.' => 'Selain langkah umum pada halaman [[A0]]Kerentanan berbasis DOM[[/A0]], hindari mengirim pesan web yang berisi data dari sumber tidak tepercaya. Saat mengirim pesan lintas origin, selalu tentukan jendela target secara eksplisit. Yang terpenting, terapkan verifikasi origin yang ketat terhadap setiap pesan masuk.',

    // document-domain-manipulation
    'DOM-based document-domain manipulation' => 'Manipulasi document.domain berbasis DOM',
    "In this section, we'll describe DOM-based manipulation of the [[C0]] property and suggest ways to reduce your exposure to this kind of attack." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami menjelaskan manipulasi properti [[C0]] berbasis DOM dan langkah mengurangi risiko serangan tersebut.',
    'What is DOM-based document-domain manipulation?' => 'Apa itu manipulasi document.domain berbasis DOM?',
    'Document-domain manipulation vulnerabilities arise when a script uses attacker-controllable data to set the [[C0]] property. An attacker may be able to use the vulnerability to construct a URL that, if visited by another user, will cause the response page to set an arbitrary [[C1]] value.' => 'Kerentanan manipulasi document.domain muncul saat skrip memakai data yang dikendalikan penyerang untuk menetapkan properti [[C0]]. Penyerang dapat menyusun URL yang, jika dibuka pengguna lain, membuat halaman respons menetapkan nilai [[C1]] sembarang.',
    'The [[C0]] property is used by browsers in their enforcement of the same origin policy. If two pages from different origins explicitly set the same [[C1]] value, then those two pages can interact in unrestricted ways. If an attacker can cause a page of a targeted website and another page they control (either directly, or via an XSS-like vulnerability) to set the same [[C2]] value, then the attacker may be able to fully compromise the target page via the page they already control. This opens up the same possibilities for exploitation as regular cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities.' => 'Properti [[C0]] dipakai browser saat menegakkan same-origin policy. Jika dua halaman dari origin berbeda menetapkan nilai [[C1]] yang sama secara eksplisit, keduanya dapat berinteraksi tanpa batas. Bila penyerang berhasil membuat halaman situs target dan halaman yang ia kendalikan (baik langsung maupun lewat celah mirip XSS) memakai nilai [[C2]] yang sama, penyerang dapat menguasai halaman target sepenuhnya melalui halaman miliknya. Kondisi ini membuka peluang eksploitasi setara kerentanan XSS biasa.',
    'Browsers generally enforce some restrictions on the values that can be assigned to [[C0]], and may prevent the use of completely different values than the actual origin of the page. However, there are two important caveats to this. Firstly, browsers allow the use of child or parent domains, so an attacker may be able to switch the domain of the target page to that of a related website with a weaker security posture. Secondly, some browser quirks enable switching to completely unrelated domains. These caveats mean that the ability to manipulate the [[C1]] property of a page generally represents a security vulnerability whose severity is not far behind regular XSS.' => 'Browser umumnya membatasi nilai yang boleh diberikan ke [[C0]] dan menolak nilai yang berbeda jauh dari origin asli halaman. Namun ada dua pengecualian penting. Pertama, browser mengizinkan penggunaan domain induk atau subdomain, sehingga penyerang bisa mengalihkan domain target ke situs terkait yang keamanannya lebih lemah. Kedua, beberapa perilaku khusus browser memungkinkan peralihan ke domain yang sama sekali tidak terkait. Oleh karena itu, kemampuan memanipulasi properti [[C1]] tetap tergolong kerentanan serius yang tingkat keparahannya mendekati XSS.',
    'Which sinks can lead to DOM-based document-domain manipulation vulnerabilities?' => 'Sink apa saja yang memicu manipulasi document.domain berbasis DOM?',
    'The [[C0]] sink can lead to DOM-based document-domain manipulation vulnerabilities.' => 'Sink [[C0]] dapat memicu kerentanan manipulasi document.domain berbasis DOM.',
    'How to prevent DOM-based document-domain manipulation vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah manipulasi document.domain berbasis DOM',
    'In addition to the general measures described on the [[A0]]DOM-based vulnerabilities[[/A0]] page, you should avoid allowing data from any untrusted source to dynamically set the [[C0]] property.' => 'Selain langkah umum pada halaman [[A0]]Kerentanan berbasis DOM[[/A0]], hindari membiarkan data dari sumber tidak tepercaya menetapkan properti [[C0]] secara dinamis.',

    // websocket-url-poisoning
    'DOM-based WebSocket-URL poisoning' => 'Peracunan URL WebSocket berbasis DOM',
    "In this section, we'll talk about how WebSocket URLs can be poisoned using DOM-based attacks, discuss the impact of WebSocket-URL poisoning, and suggest ways you can reduce your exposure to this kind of attack." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami membahas bagaimana URL WebSocket dapat diracuni lewat serangan berbasis DOM, dampaknya, serta langkah mengurangi paparan risiko.',
    'What is DOM-based WebSocket-URL poisoning?' => 'Apa itu peracunan URL WebSocket berbasis DOM?',
    "WebSocket-URL poisoning occurs when a script uses controllable data as the target URL of a WebSocket connection. An attacker may be able to use this vulnerability to construct a URL that, if visited by another user, will cause the user's browser to open a WebSocket connection to a URL that is under the attacker's control." => 'Peracunan URL WebSocket terjadi saat skrip memakai data yang dapat dikendalikan sebagai URL target koneksi WebSocket. Penyerang dapat membuat URL yang, bila dikunjungi korban, memaksa browser korban membuka koneksi WebSocket ke URL milik penyerang.',
    'What is the impact of WebSocket-URL poisoning?' => 'Apa dampak peracunan URL WebSocket?',
    "The potential impact of WebSocket-URL poisoning depends on how the website uses WebSockets. If the website transmits sensitive data from the user's browser to the WebSocket server, then the attacker may be able to capture this data." => 'Dampak potensialnya bergantung pada pemakaian WebSockets oleh situs. Jika situs mengirim data sensitif dari browser pengguna ke server WebSocket, penyerang berpeluang menyadap data tersebut.',
    "If the application reads data from the WebSocket server and processes it in some way, the attacker may be able to subvert the website's logic or deliver client-side attacks against the user." => 'Jika aplikasi membaca data dari server WebSocket lalu memprosesnya, penyerang dapat membelokkan logika situs atau mengirimkan serangan sisi klien ke pengguna.',
    'Which sinks can lead to WebSocket-URL poisoning vulnerabilities?' => 'Sink apa saja yang memicu peracunan URL WebSocket?',
    'The [[C0]] constructor can lead to WebSocket-URL poisoning vulnerabilities.' => 'Konstruktor [[C0]] dapat memicu kerentanan peracunan URL WebSocket.',
    'How to prevent DOM-based WebSocket-URL poisoning vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah peracunan URL WebSocket berbasis DOM',
    'In addition to the general measures described on the [[A0]]DOM-based vulnerabilities[[/A0]] page, you should avoid allowing data from any untrusted source to dynamically set the target URL of a WebSocket connection.' => 'Selain langkah umum pada halaman [[A0]]Kerentanan berbasis DOM[[/A0]], hindari membiarkan data dari sumber tidak tepercaya menentukan URL target koneksi WebSocket secara dinamis.',

    // cookie-manipulation
    'DOM-based cookie manipulation' => 'Manipulasi cookie berbasis DOM',
    "In this section, we'll describe DOM-based cookie manipulation, look at what impact it can have, and suggest ways to reduce your exposure to cookie-manipulation vulnerabilities." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami menjelaskan manipulasi cookie berbasis DOM, meninjau dampaknya, dan menyarankan cara mengurangi risiko kerentanan tersebut.',
    'What is DOM-based cookie manipulation?' => 'Apa itu manipulasi cookie berbasis DOM?',
    'Some DOM-based vulnerabilities allow attackers to manipulate data that they do not typically control. This transforms normally-safe data types, such as cookies, into potential sources. DOM-based cookie-manipulation vulnerabilities arise when a script writes attacker-controllable data into the value of a cookie.' => 'Sebagian kerentanan berbasis DOM memungkinkan penyerang memanipulasi data yang lazimnya tidak mereka kendalikan, sehingga tipe data yang normalnya aman seperti cookie ikut berubah menjadi source potensial. Celah manipulasi cookie berbasis DOM muncul saat skrip menulis data kendali penyerang ke nilai sebuah cookie.',
    "An attacker may be able to use this vulnerability to construct a URL that, if visited by another user, will set an arbitrary value in the user's cookie. Many sinks are largely harmless on their own, but DOM-based cookie-manipulation attacks demonstrate how low-severity vulnerabilities can sometimes be used as part of an exploit chain for a high-severity attack. For example, if JavaScript writes data from a source into [[C0]] without sanitizing it first, an attacker can manipulate the value of a single cookie to inject arbitrary values:" => 'Penyerang dapat memanfaatkan celah ini lewat URL yang, bila dibuka pengguna lain, menyetel nilai sembarang pada cookie korban. Banyak sink terlihat sepele jika berdiri sendiri, tetapi serangan manipulasi cookie membuktikan bagaimana celah berdampak rendah bisa dirangkai menjadi serangan berisiko tinggi. Misalnya, jika JavaScript menulis data dari source ke [[C0]] tanpa sanitasi, penyerang bisa menyisipkan nilai sembarang ke dalam cookie:',
    'If the website unsafely reflects values from cookies without HTML-encoding them, an attacker can use cookie-manipulation techniques to exploit this behavior.' => 'Jika situs memantulkan nilai cookie tanpa HTML encoding yang aman, penyerang dapat memakai teknik manipulasi cookie untuk mengeksploitasinya.',
    'What is the impact of a DOM-based cookie-manipulation attack?' => 'Apa dampak serangan manipulasi cookie berbasis DOM?',
    "The potential impact of this vulnerability depends on the role that the cookie plays within the website. If the cookie is used to control the behavior that results from certain user actions (for example, a production versus demo mode setting), then the attacker may be able to cause the user to perform unintended actions by manipulating the cookie's value." => 'Dampaknya bergantung pada peran cookie di dalam situs. Jika cookie mengatur perilaku fitur tertentu (misalnya mode produksi versus mode demo), penyerang bisa membuat pengguna menjalankan aksi tak diinginkan dengan mengubah nilai cookie tersebut.',
    "If the cookie is used to track the user's session, then the attacker may be able to perform a session fixation attack, in which they set the cookie's value to a valid token that they have obtained from the website, and then hijack the session during the victim's subsequent interaction with the website. A cookie-manipulation vulnerability like this can be used to attack not only the vulnerable website, but any other website under the same parent domain." => 'Jika cookie dipakai untuk melacak sesi pengguna, penyerang dapat melakukan serangan session fixation dengan menyetel cookie ke token valid miliknya lalu membajak sesi ketika korban berinteraksi berikutnya. Celah seperti ini tidak hanya mengancam situs rentan, tetapi juga situs lain di bawah domain induk yang sama.',
    'Which sinks can lead to DOM-based cookie-manipulation vulnerabilities?' => 'Sink apa saja yang memicu manipulasi cookie berbasis DOM?',
    'The [[C0]] sink can lead to DOM-based cookie-manipulation vulnerabilities.' => 'Sink [[C0]] dapat memicu kerentanan manipulasi cookie berbasis DOM.',
    'How to prevent DOM-based cookie-manipulation vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah manipulasi cookie berbasis DOM',
    'In addition to the general measures described on the [[A0]]DOM-based vulnerabilities[[/A0]] page, you should avoid dynamically writing to cookies using data that originated from any untrusted source.' => 'Selain langkah umum pada halaman [[A0]]Kerentanan berbasis DOM[[/A0]], hindari menulis nilai ke cookie secara dinamis memakai data dari sumber tidak tepercaya.',

    // open-redirection
    'DOM-based open redirection' => 'Open redirection berbasis DOM',
    "In this section, we'll talk about what DOM-based open redirection is, demonstrate how an attack is constructed, and suggest ways to reduce your exposure to DOM-based open-redirection vulnerabilities." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami menjelaskan apa itu DOM-based open redirection, menunjukkan cara menyusun serangannya, dan menyarankan cara mengurangi risikonya.',
    'What is DOM-based open redirection?' => 'Apa itu DOM-based open redirection?',
    'DOM-based open-redirection vulnerabilities arise when a script writes attacker-controllable data into a sink that can trigger cross-domain navigation. For example, the following code is vulnerable due to the unsafe way it handles the [[C0]] property:' => 'Kerentanan DOM-based open redirection muncul saat skrip menulis data yang dikendalikan penyerang ke sink yang memicu navigasi lintas domain. Misalnya, kode berikut rentan karena menangani properti [[C0]] secara tidak aman:',
    'An attacker may be able to use this vulnerability to construct a URL that, if visited by another user, will cause a redirection to an arbitrary external domain.' => 'Penyerang dapat menyusun URL yang, jika dikunjungi pengguna lain, memicu pengalihan ke domain eksternal sembarang.',
    'What is the impact of DOM-based open redirection?' => 'Apa dampak DOM-based open redirection?',
    'This behavior can be leveraged to facilitate phishing attacks against users of the website, for example. The ability to use an authentic application URL targeting the correct domain and with a valid TLS certificate (if TLS is used) lends credibility to the phishing attack because many users, even if they verify these features, will not notice the subsequent redirection to a different domain.' => 'Perilaku ini sering dimanfaatkan untuk melancarkan serangan phishing terhadap pengguna situs. Pemakaian URL aplikasi asli dengan domain resmi dan sertifikat TLS valid memberi kesan meyakinkan, karena banyak pengguna tidak menyadari pengalihan lanjutan ke domain lain.',
    'If an attacker is able to control the start of the string that is passed to the redirection API, then it may be possible to escalate this vulnerability into a JavaScript injection attack. An attacker could construct a URL with the [[C0]] pseudo-protocol to execute arbitrary code when the URL is processed by the browser.' => 'Jika penyerang mengendalikan awal string yang diteruskan ke API pengalihan, celah ini bisa ditingkatkan menjadi injeksi JavaScript. Penyerang cukup membuat URL berawalan pseudo-protokol [[C0]] agar browser mengeksekusi kode sembarang saat URL diproses.',
    'Which sinks can lead to DOM-based open-redirection vulnerabilities?' => 'Sink apa saja yang memicu DOM-based open redirection?',
    'The following are some of the main sinks can lead to DOM-based open-redirection vulnerabilities:' => 'Berikut beberapa sink utama yang dapat memicu kerentanan DOM-based open redirection:',
    'How to prevent DOM-based open-redirection vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah DOM-based open redirection',
    'In addition to the general measures described in the [[A0]]DOM-vulnerabilities[[/A0]] topic, you should avoid dynamically setting redirection targets using data that originated from any untrusted source.' => 'Selain langkah umum pada topik [[A0]]Kerentanan berbasis DOM[[/A0]], hindari menyetel tujuan pengalihan secara dinamis memakai data dari sumber tidak tepercaya.',
    'URL validation bypass cheat sheet' => 'Contekan bypass validasi URL',

    // controlling-the-web-message-source
    'Controlling the web message source' => 'Mengendalikan sumber web message',
    "In this section, we'll look at how web messages can be used as a source to exploit DOM-based vulnerabilities on the recipient page. We'll also describe how such an attack is constructed, including how common origin-verification techniques can often be bypassed." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami membahas bagaimana web message dapat dimanfaatkan sebagai source untuk mengeksploitasi kerentanan berbasis DOM di halaman penerima, termasuk cara teknik verifikasi origin yang umum sering dilewati.',
    'If a page handles incoming web messages in an unsafe way, for example, by not verifying the origin of incoming messages correctly in the event listener, properties and functions that are called by the event listener can potentially become sinks. For example, an attacker could host a malicious [[C0]] and use the [[C1]] method to pass web message data to the vulnerable event listener, which then sends the payload to a sink on the parent page. This behavior means that you can use web messages as the source for propagating malicious data to any of those sinks.' => 'Jika halaman menangani pesan web masuk secara tidak aman, misalnya tidak memverifikasi origin pengirim dengan benar di event listener, properti dan fungsi yang dipanggil di dalamnya berpotensi menjadi sink. Penyerang dapat membuat [[C0]] berbahaya lalu memakai metode [[C1]] untuk mengirim payload ke event listener rentan hingga mencapai sink di halaman induk. Dengan begitu, web message menjadi source untuk mengalirkan data berbahaya ke berbagai sink.',
    'What is the impact of DOM-based web message vulnerabilities?' => 'Apa dampak kerentanan web message berbasis DOM?',
    "The potential impact of the vulnerability depends on the destination document's handling of the incoming message. If the destination document trusts the sender not to transmit malicious data in the message, and handles the data in an unsafe way by passing it into a sink, then the joint behavior of the two documents may allow an attacker to compromise the user, for example." => 'Dampaknya bergantung pada cara dokumen tujuan memproses pesan masuk. Jika dokumen penerima memercayai pengirim dan langsung meneruskan pesan ke sink tanpa pemeriksaan aman, kombinasi kedua dokumen dapat memungkinkan penyerang mengambil alih sesi pengguna.',
    'How to construct an attack using web messages as the source' => 'Cara menyusun serangan dengan web message sebagai source',
    'Consider the following code:' => 'Perhatikan kode berikut:',
    'This is vulnerable because an attacker could inject a JavaScript payload by constructing the following [[C0]]:' => 'Kode di atas rentan karena penyerang dapat menyuntikkan payload JavaScript melalui [[C0]] berikut:',
    'As the event listener does not verify the origin of the message, and the [[C0]] method specifies the [[C1]] [[C2]], the event listener accepts the payload and passes it into a sink, in this case, the [[C3]] function.' => 'Karena event listener tidak memeriksa origin pesan dan metode [[C0]] menetapkan [[C1]] [[C2]], listener menerima payload dan meneruskannya ke sink berupa fungsi [[C3]].',
    'Origin verification' => 'Verifikasi origin',
    'Even if an event listener does include some form of origin verification, this verification step can sometimes be fundamentally flawed. For example, consider the following code:' => 'Meskipun event listener sudah menyertakan verifikasi origin, implementasinya tetap bisa cacat secara mendasar. Perhatikan contoh berikut:',
    'The [[C0]] method is used to try and verify that the origin of the incoming message is the [[C1]] domain. However, in practice, it only checks whether the string [[C2]] is contained anywhere in the origin URL. As a result, an attacker could easily bypass this verification step if the origin of their malicious message was [[C3]], for example.' => 'Metode [[C0]] dipakai untuk memeriksa apakah origin pesan masuk berasal dari domain [[C1]]. Namun pada praktiknya, metode ini hanya mengecek apakah string [[C2]] muncul di bagian mana saja dari URL origin. Akibatnya, penyerang dapat melewatinya dengan mudah memakai origin seperti [[C3]].',
    'The same flaw also applies to verification checks that rely on the [[C0]] or [[C1]] methods. For example, the following event listener would regard the origin [[C2]] as safe:' => 'Cacat serupa juga berlaku pada pemeriksaan yang mengandalkan metode [[C0]] atau [[C1]]. Contohnya, event listener berikut akan menganggap origin [[C2]] sebagai origin aman:',
    'Which sinks can lead to DOM-based web message vulnerabilities?' => 'Sink apa saja yang dapat memicu kerentanan web message berbasis DOM?',
    'As long as a website accepts web message data from an untrusted source due to a lack of adequate origin verification, any sinks that are used by the incoming message event listener could potentially lead to vulnerabilities.' => 'Selama situs menerima data web message dari sumber tidak tepercaya akibat lemahnya verifikasi origin, setiap sink yang dipakai di dalam event listener berpotensi memicu kerentanan.',

    // javascript-injection
    'DOM-based JavaScript injection' => 'Injeksi JavaScript berbasis DOM',
    "In this section, we'll talk about DOM-based JavaScript-injection vulnerabilities, discuss how they can impact the victim, and suggest ways to reduce your exposure to JavaScript-injection vulnerabilities." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami membahas kerentanan injeksi JavaScript berbasis DOM, dampaknya bagi korban, serta cara mengurangi paparan terhadap serangan tersebut.',
    'What is DOM-based JavaScript injection?' => 'Apa itu injeksi JavaScript berbasis DOM?',
    "DOM-based JavaScript-injection vulnerabilities arise when a script executes attacker-controllable data as JavaScript. An attacker may be able to use the vulnerability to construct a URL that, if visited by another user, will cause arbitrary JavaScript supplied by the attacker to execute in the context of the user's browser session." => 'Kerentanan injeksi JavaScript berbasis DOM muncul saat skrip mengeksekusi data yang dikendalikan penyerang sebagai kode JavaScript. Penyerang dapat membuat URL yang, jika dibuka pengguna lain, mengeksekusi JavaScript sembarang di dalam konteks sesi browser korban.',
    "Users can be induced to visit the attacker's malicious URL in various ways, similar to the usual attack-delivery vectors for reflected cross-site scripting vulnerabilities. For more information, please refer to our page on [[A0]]DOM XSS[[/A0]]." => 'Korban dapat diarahkan mengunjungi URL berbahaya melalui berbagai cara yang mirip dengan skenario reflected cross-site scripting. Penjelasan lengkap tersedia di halaman [[A0]]DOM XSS[[/A0]].',
    'What is the impact of a DOM-based JavaScript-injection attack?' => 'Apa dampak serangan injeksi JavaScript berbasis DOM?',
    "The attacker-supplied code can perform a wide variety of actions, such as stealing the victim's session token or login credentials, performing arbitrary actions on the victim's behalf, or even logging their keystrokes." => 'Kode dari penyerang dapat melakukan berbagai aksi berbahaya, mulai dari mencuri token sesi dan kredensial login korban, menjalankan aksi sembarang atas nama korban, hingga merekam ketikan keyboard.',
    'Which sinks can lead to DOM-based JavaScript-injection vulnerabilities?' => 'Sink apa saja yang dapat memicu injeksi JavaScript berbasis DOM?',
    'The following are some of the main sinks that can lead to DOM-based JavaScript-injection vulnerabilities:' => 'Berikut beberapa sink utama yang dapat memicu kerentanan injeksi JavaScript berbasis DOM:',
    'How to prevent DOM-based JavaScript-injection vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah injeksi JavaScript berbasis DOM',
    'In addition to the general measures described on the [[A0]]DOM-based vulnerabilities[[/A0]] page, you should avoid allowing data from any untrusted source to be executed as JavaScript.' => 'Selain langkah umum pada halaman [[A0]]Kerentanan berbasis DOM[[/A0]], hindari membiarkan data dari sumber tidak tepercaya dieksekusi sebagai JavaScript.',
];
